1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,344
Good morning, I'm Whale Girl.

2
00:00:02,364 --> 00:00:04,660
Today is October 14.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:05,791
Five stories today:

4
00:00:05,811 --> 00:00:09,071
Google releases Gemini 4 Argon,

5
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:11,711
Anthropic hardens its anti-distillation defenses,

6
00:00:11,731 --> 00:00:15,111
Anthropic's red team looks at small models self-replicating,

7
00:00:15,131 --> 00:00:17,991
X bundles Grok and Cursor into one subscription,

8
00:00:18,011 --> 00:00:21,891
and NVIDIA's RTX Spark laptops.

9
00:00:21,911 --> 00:00:24,807
First, Google has released Gemini 4 Argon,

10
00:00:24,827 --> 00:00:27,479
and from October 13 it is open to developers

11
00:00:27,499 --> 00:00:29,287
and enterprises globally.

12
00:00:29,307 --> 00:00:31,718
Google AI Ultra and Pro subscribers

13
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:33,240
can use it in the Gemini app

14
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:35,419
and in AI Mode in Search.

15
00:00:35,439 --> 00:00:38,325
The introductory API price, per million tokens,

16
00:00:38,345 --> 00:00:41,200
is $2 for input and $10 for output.

17
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,551
The introductory period ends on November 30,

18
00:00:43,571 --> 00:00:47,171
after which it rises to $4 input and $20 output.

19
00:00:47,191 --> 00:00:49,515
The context limit is 1 million tokens,

20
00:00:49,535 --> 00:00:52,022
counted across input and output combined.

21
00:00:52,042 --> 00:00:55,228
Google says it ranks first on the Vals Index,

22
00:00:55,248 --> 00:00:59,218
which covers finance, coding, legal and tax work.

23
00:00:59,238 --> 00:01:02,479
It scores 87% on the ERQA embodied reasoning benchmark,

24
00:01:02,499 --> 00:01:05,844
which Google says beats other frontier models.

25
00:01:05,864 --> 00:01:09,325
Google also says that on the Gray Swan benchmark,

26
00:01:09,345 --> 00:01:11,099
the indirect prompt injection

27
00:01:11,119 --> 00:01:13,567
attack success rate is down to 0.7%.

28
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:14,820
Also, 10,000 scientists

29
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,640
can use Antigravity free

30
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,313
for six months at the highest usage tier,

31
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:22,123
subject to eligibility and selection.

32
00:01:22,143 --> 00:01:24,919
These results are all published by Google itself.

33
00:01:25,119 --> 00:01:26,620
Second, Anthropic has announced

34
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:29,240
new measures against distillation attacks.

35
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:32,915
Distillation means collecting one model's outputs in bulk

36
00:01:32,935 --> 00:01:35,232
to train another model.

37
00:01:35,252 --> 00:01:38,833
Anthropic says early evidence suggests

38
00:01:38,853 --> 00:01:41,732
the measures cut the data distillers

39
00:01:41,752 --> 00:01:44,267
can collect by around 90% to 99%.

40
00:01:44,287 --> 00:01:45,783
The first is preserved thinking:

41
00:01:45,803 --> 00:01:49,583
API accounts created on or after August 31

42
00:01:49,603 --> 00:01:52,250
cannot edit earlier context.

43
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:54,731
The second is a two-stage classifier

44
00:01:54,751 --> 00:01:56,955
with a false positive rate below 0.1%.

45
00:01:56,975 --> 00:01:59,202
The third is, for repeat extractors,

46
00:01:59,222 --> 00:02:01,921
tighter limits and bans once confirmed.

47
00:02:01,941 --> 00:02:02,982
Since September 24,

48
00:02:03,002 --> 00:02:05,727
in specific areas where false positives are under 0.1%,

49
00:02:05,747 --> 00:02:09,689
requests blocked by its safeguards are also charged for.

50
00:02:09,709 --> 00:02:14,075
One data point: a distilled model trained on full

51
00:02:14,095 --> 00:02:17,925
transcripts scores 80.4% on SWE-bench Verified,

52
00:02:17,945 --> 00:02:20,954
and drops to 71.8% with summarized reasoning only.

53
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:23,140
The trade-off: some developers

54
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,325
must update their integrations,

55
00:02:25,345 --> 00:02:26,839
and the classifier may wrongly block

56
00:02:26,859 --> 00:02:29,166
fewer than 0.1% of benign requests.

57
00:02:29,186 --> 00:02:31,917
Anthropic itself calls it a cat-and-mouse game

58
00:02:31,937 --> 00:02:34,537
and doesn't know how long the gains will last.

59
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:37,787
Third, Anthropic's Frontier Red Team

60
00:02:37,807 --> 00:02:40,082
published research saying small models

61
00:02:40,102 --> 00:02:41,798
may be months away

62
00:02:41,818 --> 00:02:44,411
from self-replicating on home devices.

63
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:46,826
The devices are IoT gear like smart ovens

64
00:02:46,846 --> 00:02:49,862
and off-brand Android TV boxes.

65
00:02:49,882 --> 00:02:52,165
In the experiments, a 9B model

66
00:02:52,185 --> 00:02:53,548
across 9 hardware types

67
00:02:53,568 --> 00:02:56,253
got inference running on 8 of them.

68
00:02:56,273 --> 00:02:58,324
Gemma4-26B-A4B ran on

69
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,416
15 off-brand Android TV boxes,

70
00:03:00,436 --> 00:03:01,917
about $55 each,

71
00:03:01,937 --> 00:03:04,474
at 0.39 tokens per second.

72
00:03:04,494 --> 00:03:07,070
In a simplified end-to-end replication test,

73
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:10,550
GLM-5.2 reached all 8 nodes

74
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:12,387
in 4 of 5 trials.

75
00:03:12,407 --> 00:03:14,573
The other open-weight models failed.

76
00:03:14,593 --> 00:03:16,895
The researchers say the hacking step

77
00:03:16,915 --> 00:03:18,324
was kept trivial,

78
00:03:18,344 --> 00:03:21,104
so the results are an upper bound on real-world success.

79
00:03:21,124 --> 00:03:24,387
On a rough trend, small models by year end

80
00:03:24,407 --> 00:03:27,570
could reach GLM-5.2's replication level,

81
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:30,783
which the authors themselves call a rough estimate.

82
00:03:30,803 --> 00:03:33,143
Small models are still poor at spearphishing.

83
00:03:33,163 --> 00:03:35,073
The authors call these signs of life,

84
00:03:35,093 --> 00:03:37,179
not a full rogue replicator yet,

85
00:03:37,199 --> 00:03:39,524
and suggest network anomaly monitoring

86
00:03:39,544 --> 00:03:42,653
and ISP quarantine of infected devices.

87
00:03:42,853 --> 00:03:43,725
Fourth, X has launched

88
00:03:43,745 --> 00:03:45,764
The X Subscription,

89
00:03:45,784 --> 00:03:47,964
bundling Grok, Grok Bot,

90
00:03:47,984 --> 00:03:51,564
Cursor and X Premium into one plan.

91
00:03:51,584 --> 00:03:53,240
There are four individual paid tiers:

92
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:55,125
Plus at $8 a month,

93
00:03:55,145 --> 00:03:56,665
Premium at $30,

94
00:03:56,685 --> 00:04:00,270
Super at $100, and Ultra at $200.

95
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:02,148
X says Premium includes the benefits of

96
00:04:02,168 --> 00:04:03,556
SuperGrok,

97
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:06,776
Cursor Pro and X Premium+,

98
00:04:06,796 --> 00:04:09,646
which previously cost $90 a month combined.

99
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:12,787
On usage, Premium is 4x Plus,

100
00:04:12,807 --> 00:04:16,606
Super is 15x, and Ultra is 50x.

101
00:04:16,626 --> 00:04:19,962
Grok and Cursor share one usage pool.

102
00:04:19,982 --> 00:04:20,743
The page says

103
00:04:20,763 --> 00:04:23,823
each paid tier's coding usage with Grok models

104
00:04:23,843 --> 00:04:26,543
is at least twice the comparable Cursor plan's.

105
00:04:26,563 --> 00:04:29,154
There is also a free tier with daily Grok access

106
00:04:29,174 --> 00:04:31,647
and a starter Cursor coding allowance.

107
00:04:31,667 --> 00:04:34,068
New customers can sign up from October 12,

108
00:04:34,088 --> 00:04:36,138
with a global rollout over the following few days.

109
00:04:36,158 --> 00:04:38,335
Existing subscribers can keep their current plans

110
00:04:38,355 --> 00:04:42,154
or switch, with a prorated refund for the old plan.

111
00:04:42,174 --> 00:04:44,294
Third-party models in Cursor

112
00:04:44,314 --> 00:04:47,987
are available on Premium and above, billed separately.

113
00:04:48,187 --> 00:04:51,333
Fifth, NVIDIA and Microsoft previously announced

114
00:04:51,353 --> 00:04:53,893
that laptops with RTX Spark

115
00:04:53,913 --> 00:04:55,895
go on sale October 16.

116
00:04:55,915 --> 00:04:58,826
RTX Spark is a single superchip

117
00:04:58,846 --> 00:05:01,166
with up to 128GB of unified memory

118
00:05:01,186 --> 00:05:03,992
and 1 petaflop of AI compute.

119
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:06,966
NVIDIA's post doesn't mention pricing.

120
00:05:06,986 --> 00:05:08,872
Local agent software was updated too,

121
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:11,025
including GitHub Copilot, Hermes,

122
00:05:11,045 --> 00:05:13,738
OpenClaw and Perplexity,

123
00:05:13,758 --> 00:05:15,302
for easier local setup.

124
00:05:15,322 --> 00:05:18,703
On models, Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B

125
00:05:18,723 --> 00:05:20,993
releases on October 15.

126
00:05:21,013 --> 00:05:21,974
In creative apps,

127
00:05:21,994 --> 00:05:25,214
NVIDIA says Adobe's optimizations are up to 2x faster,

128
00:05:25,234 --> 00:05:26,774
rolling out in phases,

129
00:05:26,794 --> 00:05:29,687
with AI optimizations in Photoshop and Premiere

130
00:05:29,707 --> 00:05:31,011
already in beta.

131
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:33,302
For developers, PyTorch,

132
00:05:33,322 --> 00:05:34,939
Python and CUDA support

133
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:38,212
for RTX Spark is already available.

134
00:05:38,232 --> 00:05:40,963
For gaming, hundreds of games are supported at launch,

135
00:05:40,983 --> 00:05:43,656
and a faster DLSS 5 model

136
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:47,956
debuts in NBA 2K27 on October 16.

137
00:05:48,156 --> 00:05:51,185
That's all for today. Sources are in the description.

138
00:05:51,205 --> 00:05:52,474
See you tomorrow.
